Chapter 6. Causal State Compression

6.1 Diagnostic Sufficiency

Let D_{t+Δ} ∈ {1, …, H} be the fault label at time t + Δ. Let Y_{0:t} be the observation history. Let Z_t = 𝒞(Y_{0:t}, G) be a compressed causal state.

Definition 6.1 (ε-sufficiency). Z_t is ε-sufficient for D_{t+Δ} given Y_{0:t} if

I(D_{t+Δ}; Y_{0:t} | Z_t) ≤ ε. (6.1)

6.2 Compression Bound

Proposition 6.1 (Sufficiency implies compression bound). [Proved]
If Z_t is ε-sufficient, then

I(D_{t+Δ}; Z_t) ≥ I(D_{t+Δ}; Y_{0:t}) − ε. (6.2)

Proof. By the chain rule for mutual information,

I(D; Y_{0:t}) = I(D; Z_t) + I(D; Y_{0:t} | Z_t). (6.3)

Under (6.1), the last term is at most ε. ∎

6.3 The Causal Compression Hypothesis

Hypothesis 6.1 (Causal Compression Hypothesis, CCH). [Hypothesized]
There exist a feature map φ and a causal graph G such that Z_t = 𝒞(φ(Y_{0:t}), G) satisfies

· (H-a) ε-sufficiency with ε ≤ ε_max: I(D_{t+Δ}; Y_{0:t} | Z_t) ≤ ε_max.
· (H-b) Compression: dim(Z_t) ≪ dim(Y_{0:t}).

Status. Hypothesis 6.1 is not proved in this document. It is a scientific claim to be tested empirically.

6.4 Rate–Distortion Formulation

Proposition 6.2 (Rate–distortion lower bound). [Cited: Cover & Thomas, Ch. 10]
The minimum achievable compression rate for ε-sufficiency is

R(ε) = min_{p(z|y): I(D;Y|Z) ≤ ε} I(Y; Z). (6.4)

Remark 6.1. Proposition 6.2 provides the theoretical lower bound against which the actual dim(Z_t) is compared. The previous draft's claim dim(Z_t) ≥ max_H I(D;H) is dimensionally incoherent (bits vs. dimensions) and is removed.

