Chapter 7. Safety Envelope for LLM Reasoning

7.1 Admissibility

Definition 7.1 (Admissible outputs). Given causal state Z_t, graph G, and constraint set C = {c₁, …, c_m}, the admissible set ℛ(Z_t, G, C) ⊆ 𝒪 consists of all outputs r such that:

· (C1) Hypothesis containment: every hypothesis named in r belongs to ℋ.
· (C2) Variable containment: every variable named in r belongs to V(G).
· (C3) Causal containment: every causal relation asserted in r corresponds to an edge in G.
· (C4) Physical consistency: every balance equation asserted in r is satisfied within the numerical tolerance of Z_t.
· (C5) Score consistency: confidence scores in r are ordered consistently with {S_i}.

7.2 Safety by Rejection

Proposition 7.1 (Safety by rejection). [Proved]
Let V: 𝒪 → {0, 1} be the indicator function V(r) = 𝟙[r ∈ ℛ(Z_t, G, C)]. Define the output policy

r* = { r_LLM if V(r_LLM) = 1,
{ r_phys otherwise, (7.1)

where r_phys is the physical posterior output. Then:

(i) r* ∈ ℛ(Z_t, G, C) always.

(ii) The operator never observes a syntactically or constraint-level inadmissible diagnosis.

Proof.
(i) If V(r_LLM) = 1, then r* = r_LLM ∈ ℛ. Otherwise r* = r_phys, which is constructed from {S_i} and satisfies (C1)–(C5) by Definition 7.1.
(ii) Immediate from (i). ∎

7.3 Non-Claims

The following are explicitly not guaranteed:

· (N1) That r_LLM names the correct fault.
· (N2) That the constraint set C is complete (covers all physical violations).
· (N3) That the operator will not be misled by a syntactically valid but physically wrong explanation.
· (N4) That I(Z_t; r_LLM) is bounded away from zero.

These remain empirical questions.

Remark 7.1 (Related work). Rejection-based safety envelopes for LLM layers in safety-critical systems are supported by the literature. The Onnes system demonstrates few-shot physics-grounded LLM fault diagnosis for dilution refrigerators, matching a supervised classifier with six labeled examples. PCM-LLM integrates four physical laws as explicit constraints for reactor fault diagnosis. These works corroborate the architectural choice of a rejection envelope, though none provides a formal proof of constraint-set completeness.

