Chapter 8. Algorithms

8.1 Full Pipeline

```
Algorithm 1: CSE-LLM Diagnostic Pipeline
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Input:  Y_{0:t}, physics model (f̃, h), graph G, constraints C,
        hypothesis set H
Output: r* — admissible diagnosis with uncertainty

 1: Initialize MHE state x̂_0 and arrival cost Γ_0
 2: Initialize R-UPF with N particles {x_0^{(i)}, 1/N}
 3: G ← physical_topology()
 4: for k = 1, 2, ... do
 5:     y_k ← acquire_sensors()
 6:     r_O ← rank(𝒪(x̂_{k-1}))                  // Theorem 4.1
 7:     if dα_i ∉ 𝒪(x̂_{k-1}) then request_probe_input() // Corollary 4.1
 8:     if single_phase(x̂_{k-1}) then
 9:         x̂_k ← MHE(y_{k-N+1:k}, Γ_k)          // Algorithm 2
10:     else
11:         x̂_k ← R-UPF(y_{k-N+1:k}, N)           // Algorithm 3
12:     end if
13:     F_k ← φ(x̂_k)
14:     Z_k ← C(F_{0:k}, G)                       // Section 6
15:     A_k ← D(Z_k, Z_nominal)
16:     if A_k ≤ τ then continue
17:     for each H_i ∈ H do
18:         S_i ← score(H_i, Z_k, C)
19:         U_i ← uncertainty(H_i, Z_k)
20:     end for
21:     π_phys ← softmax({S_i})
22:     r_LLM ← LLM_reason(Z_k, G, C, H, {S_i}, {U_i})   // Alg. 5
23:     if V(r_LLM) = 1 then r* ← r_LLM
24:     else r* ← π_phys                                 // Prop. 7.1
25:     emit(r*, π_phys, U, A_k)
26: end for
```

8.2 Moving Horizon Estimation

```
Algorithm 2: MHE (Hypotheses H1–H3, including PE condition)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Input:  y_{k-N+1:k}, u_{k-N+1:k-1}, f̃, N, Γ_k
Output: x̂_k, Γ_{k+1}

1: Warm start: x_init ← shift(x_prev_solution)
2: Solve nonlinear program:
       min J = Σ ||y_i - h(x_i)||²_R
             + Σ ||x_{i+1} - f̃(x_i, u_i)||²_Q
             + Γ_k(x_{k-N+1})
       s.t.  x ∈ K,
             m_i ≥ 0, α_i ∈ [0,1], P_i > 0
   via sparse SQP with banded Hessian.
3: x̂_k ← x_opt[N]
4: Γ_{k+1} ← approximate_arrival_cost(x_opt, P_k)
5: Verify PE condition (4.7) on current horizon.
6: return x̂_k, Γ_{k+1}
```

Complexity. With sparse SQP exploiting banded structure: O(I · N · n_x²), where I is the number of SQP iterations. For N = 10, n_x = 11, and I ≤ 5: approximately 6 × 10³ flops per step.

8.3 Regularized Unscented Particle Filter

```
Algorithm 3: R-UPF (Lemma 4.1)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Input:  y_{1:t}, N, f, h, ε, σ_ε
Output: {x_t^{(i)}, w_t^{(i)}}

 1: for i = 1 to N do x_0^{(i)} ~ p_0; w_0^{(i)} = 1/N
 2: for t = 1 to T do
 3:     for i = 1 to N do
 4:         (x_pred, P_pred) ← UKF_predict(x_{t-1}^{(i)}, f)
 5:         (x_UKF, P_UKF)   ← UKF_update(x_pred, P_pred, y_t, h)
 6:         q_ε ← (1-ε) N(x_UKF, P_UKF)
 7:               + ε N(x_UKF, P_UKF + σ_ε² I)
 8:         x_t^{(i)} ~ q_ε
 9:         num ← p(y_t|x_t^{(i)}) p(x_t^{(i)}|x_{t-1}^{(i)})
10:         den ← (1-ε) N(x_t^{(i)}; x_UKF, P_UKF)
11:               + ε N(x_t^{(i)}; x_UKF, P_UKF + σ_ε² I)
12:         w_t^{(i)} ∝ w_{t-1}^{(i)} · num / den
13:     end for
14:     normalize w_t
15:     if ESS < N/2 then systematic_resample
16: end for
17: x̂_t ← Σ w_t^{(i)} x_t^{(i)}
```

