Appendix H. Operational Test for the Causal Compression Hypothesis

Hypothesis 6.1 is tested by measuring the sufficiency gap

\hat{\epsilon} = \hat{I}(D; Y_{0:t}) - \hat{I}(D; Z_t). \tag{H.1}

Two estimation strategies are used.

H.1 k-NN Information Estimator

Use the Kozachenko–Leonenko estimator on a held-out validation set. In high dimensions or multimodal posteriors, this estimator has significant bias; use KSG-style corrections and report effective sample sizes.

H.2 Operational Classifier Gap

Train two classifiers g_Y: Y_{0:t} \to D and g_Z: Z_t \to D on identical data, and measure the diagnostic-accuracy gap

\hat{\Delta}_{\text{class}} = \mathrm{Acc}(g_Y) - \mathrm{Acc}(g_Z). \tag{H.2}

This is more robust than (H.1) in high dimensions and provides a direct operational interpretation. Hypothesis 6.1 predicts \hat{\epsilon} \leq \epsilon_{\max} (or \hat{\Delta}_{\text{class}} \leq \Delta_{\max}) with 95% confidence. Rejection occurs if these bounds are exceeded.

