Appendix I. Constraint Completeness Stress Test

A novel protocol: systematically remove one balance equation or one causal edge from C or G, and measure the rate of admissible-but-incorrect diagnoses. The result is a curve

f: [0, 1] \to [0, 1] \tag{I.1}

mapping constraint-set incompleteness to residual risk. This directly quantifies the residual risk of Proposition 7.1. The protocol proceeds as follows:

1. Start with the complete constraint set C and graph G.
2. For each constraint c_j \in C, remove c_j and re-run the admissibility check on a validation set of LLM outputs.
3. Record the rate of admissible-but-incorrect diagnoses.
4. Repeat for each edge e_k \in E(G).
5. Fit the curve f and extrapolate to zero incompleteness.

